    "/api/v1/dev/pulsit/move-truck": {
      "post": {
        "description": "Stage a tracker position, then report where the truck is and what the fence says.\n\nIdempotent by construction: `stage_position` REPLACES the staged state for a device\nrather than merging into it, so pressing the same button twice leaves Redis in the\nidentical state and returns the identical response. Re-pressing is how a presenter\nrecovers from a mis-click, so it must be boring.\n\nNothing is committed. The session is used only for reads and never written to.\n\nTWO INPUT MODES (FP-197), mutually exclusive by MoveTruckRequest's own\nvalidator: `waypoint_id` (legacy, fixed Cape Town demo locations — unchanged\nbelow) or `scenario` (+ `trip_stop_id`), which computes a position relative to\nTHIS trip's own stop via orchestration/dev_truck_service.py. Whichever mode ran,\nthe EXPECTED-stop verdict fields (`precinct_id`, `distance_metres`,\n`geofence_confirmed`, ...) always describe the trip's current phase stop, exactly\nas before this task — only the TARGET fields differ by mode.",
        "operationId": "move_truck_api_v1_dev_pulsit_move_truck_post",
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/MoveTruckRequest"
              }
            }
          },
          "required": true
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/MoveTruckResponse"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful Response"
          },
          "422": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Validation Error"
          }
        },
        "security": [
          {
            "HTTPBearer": []
          }
        ],
        "summary": "Move the trip's tracker to a waypoint or a trip-stop-relative scenario (Pulsit mock state only)",
        "tags": [
          "dev-triggers"
        ]
      }
    },
